/**
 * OceanGuard — ingested real/synthetic datasets (Phase 1: data extraction only).
 * GENERATED by a one-off ingestion script from the DATASET - OCEANGUARD and DATASET 2 archives.
 * Do not hand-edit; regenerate from the sources instead. Phase 2: Modules 1 and 2 consume INGESTED_AUDIO_PROFILES, CO_LOCATED_SCENARIOS and INGESTED_AIS_LOGS via oceanGuardApi.js.
 *
 * Provenance notes
 * - INGESTED_AUDIO_PROFILES, CO_LOCATED_SCENARIOS, INGESTED_PORTS (URN fields) are SYNTHETIC scenario data.
 * - AIS timestamps are labelled UTC (MarineCadastre is UTC; CSJ timestamps carry no zone and are assumed UTC).
 * - USCG timestamps are local-naive ISO strings (no zone in source). Source column "Deficiency Code" is empty
 *   for every row, so deficiencyCode is null; use System/Subsystem/Component to classify.
 * - INGESTED_USCG_PSIX selection rule: IMO passes the 7-digit check-digit test, vessel has >=1 deficiency,
 *   ranked by (has operational control, deficiency count, inspection count, IMO), max 6 per vessel class, first 25.
 *   Operational controls are attached only when their Activity Id maps to exactly one vessel (no vessel id in source).
 * - worldPortIndex is matched by port name only (no URN port appears in the 500-row WPI subset, so it is null for all 12);
 *   portData is matched by name (Boston, Vancouver) or nearest record within 50 km (none qualified), else null.
 * - WDPA_sources_Nov2026.xlsx shares no METADATAID with the WDPA sites file, so it is not joined.
 * - search.json is a GBIF-style export with no `marine` field, so the marine===true filter keeps 0 rows from it.
 */

